# fixtures/hex/fragments/ops/variants.hex: op frames ([F06 §7.1]: tag, body length, body) of variants that store A's
# commits do not carry, back to back; decode as op frames to the end of the file. Every `prev` is taken as if the
# ops were in a Commit record at lsn 30000 (each comment gives the earlier lsn). Store A carries every op tag, a
# TextHunk and a DeleteVsModify conflict, a DanglingEdge and an ImageParse violation, the choices `value` and
# `ours`, and a DEFINE QUERY (fixtures/hex/store-a/log.1.hex). Here: the value-conflict classes FieldEdit,
# StatusFork, OwnerFieldEdited and PathClaim, conflicts on the status, observation, body, edge and schema key
# classes ([F06 §6.1], §6.2), the violation classes QueryInvalid and QueryCycle ([F19 §12.2]) with and without a
# key, the Resolve choices `theirs`, `base` and `repoint` ([F06 §7.7]), and the Schema op for a changed and a
# dropped named query ([F06 §7.6]). Node numbers, statuses ([F08 §9.5]: task 0 open, 1 in_progress, 2 done, side
# 3 deferred) and edge ids ([F08 §9.6]) are store-local; symbol ids of each class are dense in first-use order,
# named where used. U: the uid of fixtures/hex/fragments/values; D, D256, C: the digests of INDEX.md §2.

